=== REASONING (incl. rubber-duck course-corrections) ===
- VERIFICATION: rubber-duck flagged that lint can't catch unavailable/iOS-only SwiftUI APIs. FIX: CLT ships
  swiftc + the macOS SDK (with SwiftUI), and the component layer does NOT import the Shared xcframework, so
  `xcrun --sdk macosx swiftc -typecheck -target arm64-apple-macosx15.0` REALLY compiles the components here.
  Ran it after every batch — all clean. (#Preview needs Xcode's macro plugin → wrapped every preview in
  `#if DEBUG` so the swiftc gate skips them and Xcode Debug still builds them.)
- CROSS-PLATFORM: one source group builds both macOS + iOS targets. Used `#if os(iOS)/#elseif os(macOS)`
  (not bare canImport) for platform services + the iOS-only horizontalSizeClass. Clipboard is os-gated
  (UIPasteboard/NSPasteboard, @MainActor). Print + Fullscreen are CALLER-action/binding (window/context
  dependent — not faked).
- HONEST WRAPPERS: Modal/Drawer/Popover/Tooltip/Lightbox/ContextMenu are binding/action/content View
  modifiers over native presentation (the idiomatic, non-app-context-assuming pattern).
- ADAPTIVE: TSDataTable is hand-rolled (SwiftUI Table is poor on iPhone): columnar grid on macOS/regular,
  card list on compact iPhone (horizontalSizeClass-gated); stable sort (offset tie-break), Set<ID> selection
  + select-all, expansion, density, per-column Menu, bulk bar. TSRangeSlider = two native Sliders (accessible).
- A11Y: custom controls carry .isButton/.isSelected/.isHeader + accessibilityLabel/Value; no hardcoded
  user-facing strings (components take LocalizedStringKey; values rendered verbatim).
- TESTABILITY: extracted pure helpers (TSTableSort.sorted, TSCommandFilter.filter, TSCommandNavigation.move,
  TSMaskedValue.mask, TSAppearance.colorScheme) and unit-tested them.

